  "description": "Named in honor of the 1967 Cyclocross World Championships in Zurich, Switzerland, our Zurigo carries on a long tradition of delivering proven performance over varied terrains. With cyclocross racing, gravel grinding, bike commuting, credit-card touring, and back road adventure riding on the rise, now is your time to rise above on a Bianchi Zurigo. The Zurigo features a triple-butted, hydroformed aluminum frame with tubing shaped to deliver track bike acceleration and crit bike handling. A carbon fiber fork keeps the front wheel connected to the terrain while the tapered head tube provides quick and responsive steering. A Pressfit 30 bottom bracket efficiently transmits power to the rear wheel. The Zurigo’s flat bottom top tube and internal down tube cable routing makes it easy to shoulder a run-up or ford a stream. 38c clearance allows for flexibility in matching tire to terrain. Avid BB-5 disc brakes stop fast in any condition. Think of the Zurigo as the “Swiss Army Knife” of bikes.",
